Make.com Integration
Automated Emergency Alerting via Make.com WebhooksThis module handles the automated alerting pipeline
for the accident detection system. When the ESP32 detects an impact threshold via the ADXL345 accelerometer, 
it packages the crash event data and NEO-6M GPS coordinates into a JSON payload.
This payload is transmitted via an HTTP POST request to a dedicated Make.com webhook. 
The Make.com scenario then parses the incoming telemetry and routes emergency notifications 
(via Email, SMS, or Telegram) to predefined contacts, ensuring immediate alerting without
requiring a dedicated backend server.Make.com Setup Guide1. Configure the Webhook TriggerCreate a new scenario in Make.com 
and add the Webhooks module.Select Custom Webhook as the trigger.
1. create a webhook in make.com and generate the weblink .

2. Define the Data Structure (ESP32 JSON Payload)In the Make.com Webhook module, click Determine data structure.
Your ESP32 needs to send an HTTP POST request to the webhook URL containing the sensor telemetry.
Format the data as JSON so Make.com can map the variables cleanly:
JSON{
  "event": "collision_detected",
  "impact_force_g": 4.5,
  "latitude": 12.9716,
  "longitude": 77.5946,
  "google_maps_link": "https://maps.google.com/?q=12.9716,77.5946"
}
Send a single test request from your ESP32 or a tool like Postman. 
Make.com will indicate "Successfully determined" once it reads the structure.
3. Set Up the Action Module (Notification)Click the + button next to your webhook to add an action module. 
Select a communication service like Gmail (Send an Email), Twilio (Create a Message),
or Telegram.Map the parsed JSON variables directly into your message body. 
For example, your alert message can be formatted as:
CRITICAL ALER: Accident Detected!
Impact Force: {{1.impact_force_g}} GsLocation Coordinates: {{1.latitude}}, 
{{1.longitude}}View on Map: {{1.google_maps_link}}
Save the scenario, toggle the scheduling switch at the bottom left to ON, and ensure it is set to run Immediately as data arrives.
